// Title: Network Connection Initiated To DevTunnels Domain
// Sigma ID: 9501f8e6-8e3d-48fc-a8a6-1089dd5d7ef4
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Kamran Saifullah
// Date: 2023-11-20 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: exfiltration, command-and-control, T1567.001, T1572
// Description: Detects network connections to Devtunnels domains initiated by a process on a system. Attackers
//   can abuse that feature to establish a reverse shell or persistence on a machine.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of Devtunnels will also trigger this.
// References:
//   - https://blueteamops.medium.com/detecting-dev-tunnels-16f0994dc3e2
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/developer/dev-tunnels/security
//   - https://cydefops.com/devtunnels-unleashed
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/network_connection/net_connection_win_domain_devtunnels.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where RemoteUrl endswith ".devtunnels.ms"
